Subject: [seat-web] CAST(... AS SIGNED) so the migration runs on MySQL 8.4

testdata/legacy-api-v2/README.md has described this patch since Phase 19 as
"patched to `AS SIGNED` in the recorder's copy". The recorder's copy is a
clone of eveseat/web that is NOT tracked in this repository, so the patch
existed only on whichever machine last ran the recorder — and Phase 20.10
found that a fresh clone at the pinned commit gets 464 of 472 migrations,
not the documented 471.

`CAST(x AS INT)` is MariaDB's spelling; MySQL wants `SIGNED`. The query is a
data backfill over an empty table and defines no column, so the schema is
unaffected — but without the patch the migration aborts BEFORE adding
`users.main_character_id`, and seven later migrations fail in a cascade
around `users.id` / `refresh_tokens.user_id` that looks nothing like its
cause. That is exactly the kind of thing a README sentence loses and a
committed, automatically-applied patch does not.

Applied by bootstrap-legacy.sh, idempotently.

diff --git a/src/database/migrations/2019_11_12_220840_drop_groups_table.php b/src/database/migrations/2019_11_12_220840_drop_groups_table.php
index ceaf30bf..509a7969 100644
--- a/src/database/migrations/2019_11_12_220840_drop_groups_table.php
+++ b/src/database/migrations/2019_11_12_220840_drop_groups_table.php
@@ -265,7 +265,7 @@ class DropGroupsTable extends Migration
                         $join->where('user_settings.name', 'main_character_id');
                     })
                     ->whereNotNull('user_settings.value')
-                    ->selectRaw('users.group_id, users.id, users.character_owner_hash, CAST(user_settings.value AS INT)'));
+                    ->selectRaw('users.group_id, users.id, users.character_owner_hash, CAST(user_settings.value AS SIGNED)'));

         // fetch duplicated users which are not related to main character
         $entries = DB::table('mig_groups')
